{"questions":[{"question_id":"luxwdeto","content":"<p>Which of the following compounds will give silver mirror with ammoniacal silver nitrate?</p>\n<p>A. Formic acid</p>\n<p>B. Formaldehyde</p>\n<p>C. Benzaldehyde</p>\n<p>D. Acetone</p>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>","chapter":"aldehydes-ketones-and-carboxylic-acids","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-9th-april-evening-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 9th April Evening Shift","permalink":"pwhich-of-the-following-compounds-will-give-silver-mirror-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-gtj3j1tpjsinz8sw","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Which of the following compounds will give silver mirror with ammoniacal silver nitrate?</p>\n<p>A. Formic acid</p>\n<p>B. Formaldehyde</p>\n<p>C. Benzaldehyde</p>\n<p>D. Acetone</p>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"B and C only"},{"identifier":"B","content":"C and D only"},{"identifier":"C","content":"A, B and C only"},{"identifier":"D","content":"A only"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>The reaction involved here is the Tollen's test, which detects aldehydes and alpha-hydroxy ketones, as they are able to reduce the ammoniacal silver nitrate solution to metallic silver, producing a mirror-like coating on the glassware. This test specifically distinguishes these reducing sugars from non-reducing sugars and is often used to identify the presence of an aldehyde functional group. </p>\n\n<p>Let's analyze each option:</p>\n\n<p>A. Formic acid - Formic acid (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.19ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4062 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1648,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2411,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3174,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is a carboxylic acid but importantly, it can also reduce silver ions to metallic silver because it can act as a reducing agent just like aldehydes. Thus, it will give a positive Tollen's test. </p>\n\n<p>B. Formaldehyde (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.464ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 3299 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1648,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2536,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is the simplest aldehyde, and aldehydes are known to give positive results with the Tollen's test since they can be oxidized to carboxylic acids, reducing the silver ions in the process to metallic silver.</p>\n\n<p>C. Benzaldehyde (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.928ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4830.1 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1151.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2419.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3179.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4067.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is an aromatic aldehyde and, similar to formaldehyde, it can be oxidized to an acid, thereby reducing the silver ions to silver in the Tollen's test, giving a positive result.</p>\n\n<p>D. Acetone (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.62ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 5578.1 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(760,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2027.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2787.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3550.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(4310.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is a ketone. Generally, ketones do not undergo oxidation easily and do not reduce ammoniacal silver nitrate, and thus, do not give a silver mirror with the Tollen's reagent.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the compounds that will give a silver mirror with ammoniacal silver nitrate (positive Tollen's test) are Formic acid, Formaldehyde, and Benzaldehyde, but not Acetone.</p>\n\n<p>The correct answer from the options given is therefore:</p>\n\n<p>Option C: A, B, and C only.</p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>निम्नलिखित यौगिकों में से कौन अमोनिएकल सिल्वर नाइट्रेट के साथ रजत दर्पण देता है:</p>\n<p>A. फार्मिक अम्ल</p>\n<p>B. फार्मल्डिहाइड</p>\n<p>C. बेन्जैल्डिहाइड</p>\n<p>D. ऐसीटोन</p>\n<p>नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सही उत्तर चुनेः</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"केवल B एवं C"},{"identifier":"B","content":"केवल C एवं D\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"केवल A, B एवं C\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"केवल A\n"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>यहाँ शामिल अभिक्रिया टॉलेन परीक्षण है, जो एल्डिहाइड और अल्फा-हाइड्रॉक्सी कीटोन का पता लगाता है, क्योंकि ये अमोनियायुक्त सिल्वर नाइट्रेट विलयन को धात्विक सिल्वर में अपचयित कर सकते हैं, जिससे कांच के बर्तन पर दर्पण जैसी परत बनती है। यह परीक्षण विशेष रूप से इन अपचायक शर्कराओं को गैर-अपचायक शर्कराओं से अलग करता है और अक्सर एल्डिहाइड क्रियात्मक समूह की उपस्थिति की पहचान करने के लिए उपयोग किया जाता है।</p>\n\n<p>आइए प्रत्येक विकल्प का विश्लेषण करें:</p>\n\n<p>A. फॉर्मिक अम्ल - फॉर्मिक अम्ल (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.19ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4062 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1648,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2411,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3174,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) एक कार्बोक्सिलिक अम्ल है लेकिन महत्वपूर्ण रूप से, यह सिल्वर आयनों को धात्विक सिल्वर में अपचयित भी कर सकता है क्योंकि यह एल्डिहाइड की तरह अपचायक के रूप में कार्य कर सकता है। इस प्रकार, यह सकारात्मक टॉलेन परीक्षण देगा।</p>\n\n<p>B. फॉर्मेल्डिहाइड (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.464ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 3299 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1648,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2536,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) सबसे सरल एल्डिहाइड है, और एल्डिहाइड टॉलेन परीक्षण के साथ सकारात्मक परिणाम देने के लिए जाने जाते हैं क्योंकि वे कार्बोक्सिलिक अम्लों में ऑक्सीकृत हो सकते हैं, इस प्रक्रिया में सिल्वर आयनों को धात्विक सिल्वर में अपचयित करते हैं।</p>\n\n<p>C. बेंजैल्डिहाइड (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.928ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4830.1 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1151.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2419.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3179.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4067.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) एक ऐरोमैटिक एल्डिहाइड है और फॉर्मेल्डिहाइड के समान, यह अम्ल में ऑक्सीकृत हो सकता है, जिससे टॉलेन परीक्षण में सिल्वर आयनों को सिल्वर में अपचयित किया जाता है, जो सकारात्मक परिणाम देता है।</p>\n\n<p>D. एसीटोन (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.62ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 5578.1 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(760,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2027.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2787.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3550.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(4310.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) एक कीटोन है। सामान्यतः, कीटोन आसानी से ऑक्सीकरण नहीं करते हैं और अमोनियायुक्त सिल्वर नाइट्रेट को अपचयित नहीं करते हैं, और इस प्रकार, टॉलेन अभिकर्मक के साथ सिल्वर दर्पण नहीं देते हैं।</p>\n\n<p>इसलिए, वे यौगिक जो अमोनियायुक्त सिल्वर नाइट्रेट के साथ सिल्वर दर्पण देंगे (सकारात्मक टॉलेन परीक्षण) वे हैं फॉर्मिक अम्ल, फॉर्मेल्डिहाइड, और बेंजैल्डिहाइड, लेकिन एसीटोन नहीं।</p>\n\n<p>दिए गए विकल्पों में से सही उत्तर इसलिए है:</p>\n\n<p>विकल्प C: केवल A, B, और C।</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"tests-for-aldehyde-and-ketones","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["multi_statements"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-9th-april-evening-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"B and C only"},{"identifier":"B","content":"C and D only"},{"identifier":"C","content":"A, B and C only"},{"identifier":"D","content":"A only"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>The reaction involved here is the Tollen's test, which detects aldehydes and alpha-hydroxy ketones, as they are able to reduce the ammoniacal silver nitrate solution to metallic silver, producing a mirror-like coating on the glassware. This test specifically distinguishes these reducing sugars from non-reducing sugars and is often used to identify the presence of an aldehyde functional group. </p>\n\n<p>Let's analyze each option:</p>\n\n<p>A. Formic acid - Formic acid (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.19ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4062 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1648,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2411,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3174,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is a carboxylic acid but importantly, it can also reduce silver ions to metallic silver because it can act as a reducing agent just like aldehydes. Thus, it will give a positive Tollen's test. </p>\n\n<p>B. Formaldehyde (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.464ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 3299 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1648,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2536,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is the simplest aldehyde, and aldehydes are known to give positive results with the Tollen's test since they can be oxidized to carboxylic acids, reducing the silver ions in the process to metallic silver.</p>\n\n<p>C. Benzaldehyde (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.928ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4830.1 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1151.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2419.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3179.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4067.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is an aromatic aldehyde and, similar to formaldehyde, it can be oxidized to an acid, thereby reducing the silver ions to silver in the Tollen's test, giving a positive result.</p>\n\n<p>D. Acetone (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.62ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 5578.1 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(760,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2027.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2787.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3550.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(4310.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is a ketone. Generally, ketones do not undergo oxidation easily and do not reduce ammoniacal silver nitrate, and thus, do not give a silver mirror with the Tollen's reagent.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the compounds that will give a silver mirror with ammoniacal silver nitrate (positive Tollen's test) are Formic acid, Formaldehyde, and Benzaldehyde, but not Acetone.</p>\n\n<p>The correct answer from the options given is therefore:</p>\n\n<p>Option C: A, B, and C only.</p>"}]}